      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "BREEZIN' (3) was a close-up fourth two back then a bit plain last time over 1200m at Ipswich, finishing 3.5 lengths away in sixth after being in contention on the bend. This doesn't look as hard so she is well worth another chance. GOOSE STEP (9) was a Dalby winner six back then has placed in five runs since, the latest finishing a 0.7 lengths second at Esk. This is no easier but drops in weight and is honest. I'M LUCKY TWO (8) resumed off a long break over 1000m at this track and was only beaten 1.75 lengths into fourth. Likely improver from the run and looks well placed here. Strong prospects. WANTED HILLBILLY (2) resumes in a similar race to his last run 11 weeks ago when sixth, beaten 4 lengths. Has switched to the Kristie Clark-Peoples stable. Expecting a strong run fresh. MA'S EPIC (5) has been a while since a win but is going better than form reads and is worth including.",
